<!--
  Where a session's levels are read (ADR-0018). Served beside the engine's
  interface, on the same object, by reverblabrd.

  **Not public** (ADR-0020): a handshake between reverblabrd and the window
  of the same build, which may change in any release. The memory it hands
  out carries a fingerprint of its layout, so a window of another build
  refuses it rather than misreading it.

  **Not part of the engine's API**, and apart from it on purpose: telemetry
  never travels as messages (ADR-0003). This interface hands a window, once,
  the memory the levels are published in; from then on the window reads
  them on its own frame tick and nothing is sent at all.

  **The one method here returns a value**, which the engine's never do: a
  descriptor has to be answered to whoever asked, and a signal would hand it
  to every window on the bus.
-->
<node>
  <interface name="io.github.reverblabr.Telemetry">

    <!--
      A read-only descriptor for the shared memory that sessionId's
      snapshots are published in: a sealed memfd holding a TelemetryRegion
      (engine/core/sharedtelemetry.h), which starts with its magic number,
      version and a fingerprint of its layout. It stays valid for as long as
      the caller keeps it or a mapping of it, and it is what the session
      publishes into for as long as the session is open; a session opened
      again after it closed is new memory, to be asked for again.

      Fails with io.github.reverblabr.Error.NoTelemetry when no session of
      that id is open.
    -->
    <method name="Share">
      <arg name="sessionId" type="s" direction="in"/>
      <arg name="memory" type="h" direction="out"/>
    </method>

  </interface>
</node>
